                                    <h1>Klaviyo vs Braze vs Iterable: D2C Marketing Automation Comparison 2026</h1>
                                    <p>Beyond Klaviyo + WebEngage + MoEngage (mid-market comparison already covered), enterprise D2C brands + scaled D2C tech companies increasingly evaluate Klaviyo vs Braze vs Iterable — three leading enterprise-grade marketing automation platforms. Different strengths + pricing + scale-stage fit. Here is the honest comparison for 2026-2027.</p>
                                    <h2>Platform Overview + Positioning</h2>
                                    <p><strong>Klaviyo:</strong> D2C-native + Shopify-integrated + email-primary + growing SMS + expanded channels + mid-market to enterprise growth.<br><strong>Braze:</strong> Enterprise mobile-first + push + in-app + email + full omnichannel + higher-scale enterprise focus.<br><strong>Iterable:</strong> Enterprise data-driven + email + SMS + push + in-app + workflow + strong customer-data-focused + mid-market to enterprise.</p>
                                    <h2>Feature Comparison</h2>
                                    <p><strong>Email:</strong> Klaviyo strongest for D2C + Shopify. Braze + Iterable strong.<br><strong>SMS:</strong> Klaviyo strong USA + growing. Braze + Iterable strong.<br><strong>Push notifications:</strong> Braze strongest for mobile-first + app-based businesses. Iterable strong. Klaviyo growing.<br><strong>In-app messaging:</strong> Braze strongest. Iterable strong. Klaviyo limited.<br><strong>Segmentation:</strong> All three strong. Iterable strongest for complex data-driven segmentation.<br><strong>AI / personalisation:</strong> All three growing rapidly. Braze + Iterable slightly ahead.<br><strong>Shopify integration:</strong> Klaviyo deepest. Braze + Iterable strong.<br><strong>Enterprise / scale features:</strong> Braze + Iterable more mature. Klaviyo growing enterprise.</p>
                                    <h2>Pricing Comparison</h2>
                                    <p><strong>Klaviyo:</strong> $60-3,000+ / month based on list size. Transparent pricing tier.<br><strong>Braze:</strong> Custom enterprise pricing — typically $2,000-50,000+ / month based on monthly active users + features.<br><strong>Iterable:</strong> Custom enterprise pricing — typically $3,000-40,000+ / month based on contacts + features.<br>Klaviyo more accessible mid-market. Braze + Iterable enterprise-focused pricing.</p>
                                    <h2>When to Choose Each</h2>
                                    <p><strong>Choose Klaviyo if:</strong> D2C brand + Shopify-heavy + email-primary + mid-market to growth-stage + transparent pricing preferred + strong Shopify integration matters.<br><strong>Choose Braze if:</strong> Mobile-first D2C + app-based business + push + in-app critical + enterprise scale + omnichannel + custom pricing acceptable.<br><strong>Choose Iterable if:</strong> Data-driven marketing team + complex segmentation + workflow-heavy + enterprise + customer data platform integration + high scale.</p>
                                    <h2>Migration Complexity</h2>
                                    <p>Migration between platforms increases with enterprise scale:<br><strong>Klaviyo → Braze / Iterable:</strong> 3-6 months typical enterprise migration.<br><strong>Braze ↔ Iterable:</strong> 4-8 months enterprise migration.<br><strong>Data migration:</strong> Customer + subscriber + segmentation + workflow rebuild.<br><strong>Template + creative rebuild:</strong> Email + push + in-app template rebuild.<br><strong>Integration reconfiguration:</strong> Shopify + CDP + analytics + other integrations.<br>Migration cost + risk significant — choose carefully upfront + commit 3+ years minimum.</p>
                                    <h2>Hybrid + Best-of-Breed Reality</h2>
                                    <p>Some enterprise D2C brands run hybrid approaches:<br><strong>Klaviyo for email + Braze for mobile</strong> — best-of-breed per channel.<br><strong>Iterable + CDP integration</strong> — data-heavy setup.<br><strong>Multiple regional platforms</strong> — Klaviyo USA + WebEngage / MoEngage India + regional variations.<br>Hybrid works but creates data + attribution + operational complexity. Unified platform simpler where possible.</p>

